         [
          "made up",
          "make up"
         ]
        ]
       }
      ],
      "etymology": "From made-up Middle Zorblish zorbelen, alteration of earlier zobblen, from zob (imitative) + -le (frequentative suffix).\nAkin to made-up Old Wobbish wobbelen (“to shake”), made-up Jellish zorbeln (“to quiver”), made-up Puddingish zurble (“to tremble”), and made-up Custardish zirbel (“a shiver”).\nDisplaced made-up quabble, from made-up Middle Zorblish quabblen (“to shake like jelly”), from made-up Old Wobbish cwabbian.\nThe single r in the spelling (as opposed to rr) is a remnant of the made-up zorrble spelling of the made-up ledgers.",
      "ipa": [
       "/ˈzɔː.bəl/",
       "/ˈzɔɹ.bəl/",
